      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes **how the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure**. Specifically:\n\n- Before any file is overwritten, the guarded tool executor records the file\u0027s prior state in an in-memory write journal \u2014 either its previous content (if it existed) or the fact that it didn\u0027t exist.\n- If a run fails (due to turn cap, unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal can roll all recorded writes back in reverse order, restoring previous content or deleting newly created files.\n- This approach gives each run all-or-nothing semantics without needing a database transaction \u2014 the journal itself acts as the transaction log, existing only in process memory for the duration of one run.\n- The Query agent doesn\u0027t use the rollback path since it has no write tool, though the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library.",
